  ## **2\. n8n** — best for flexible, multi-step automations across tools and APIs
  
  ![n8n interface](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/69297a3b020bb78b3d249dc9_n8n-interface.webp)
  
  [n8n](https://n8n.io/) platform interface
  
  n8n is a workflow automation platform that lets teams connect apps, APIs, and processes into custom automated workflows using a visual builder. Unlike simpler automation tools that bill by action or user, n8n lets you design complex sequences without step limits and connect across hundreds of systems. Its strength is flexibility: you can use built-in nodes, custom code, and advanced logic to automate cross-tool work that would otherwise take hours to manage manually. It’s ideal for teams with integration needs that go beyond basic trigger-and-action automations.
  
  ### **n8n pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Native Softr integration:** A verified Softr node in n8n lets you connect Softr Databases directly in workflows to create, update, get, or delete records and manage users without manual API wiring.
  - **Unlimited workflows & users:** Every paid tier includes unlimited workflows, unlimited steps, and unlimited users so teams can scale freely.
  - **Open-source option:** The Community Edition is free to use if self-hosted, giving teams full control over automation without licensing fees.
  - **400+ integrations:** Connect a broad range of services (CRMs, databases, messaging, cloud apps) with no extra add-ons.
  - **Technical flexibility:** Native JavaScript and Python support lets dev teams extend workflows with custom logic.
  - **Self-hosted or cloud:** Choose between self-managed infrastructure or a hosted cloud instance based on your compliance and budget needs.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **Steep learning curve for non-technical teams:** The visual builder is powerful, but mastering complex flows often requires technical fluency.
  - **Hosting and setup overhead:** The free self-hosted version requires server provisioning, scaling, and maintenance, which adds operational work many teams don’t want.
  - **Execution-based pricing can add up:** Cloud plans charge by workflow executions per month, meaning frequent automations can increase costs faster than flat-rate tools.
  
  ### **n8n best features**
  
  - **Visual workflow builder:** Drag-and-drop nodes let you stitch together multi-step, cross-app processes.
  - **Open-source Community Edition:** Free forever if self-hosted—no license limits on workflows or users.
  - **Cloud plans with unlimited users & steps:** Managed hosting starts with execution quotas, not user caps.
  - **Extensive integrations:** Connect common business tools and custom APIs via HTTP Request nodes.
  - **Custom code support:** Inject JavaScript or Python directly into workflows for tailored logic.
  
  ### **N8n pricing**
  
  All plans include unlimited users & workflows and every integration.
  
  Pricing based on monthly workflow executions, regardless of complexity
  
  - **Free** open-source community edition
  - **Starter:** $20/month (billed annually) hosted by n8n, includes 2.5k workflow executions/month, unlimited steps, unlimited users, and up to 5 concurrent executions.
  - **Pro:** $50/month (billed annually) hosted by n8n, includes 10k workflow executions/month, higher concurrency (20 concurrent executions), shared projects, admin roles, execution history, and workflow insights.
  - **Business:** $800/month (billed annually) self-hosted, includes 40k workflow executions/month, SSO (SAML/LDAP), multiple environments, version control (Git), scaling options, and longer execution insights.
  - **Enterprise:** custom pricing, self-hosted or hosted by n8n. Unlimited shared projects, **200+ concurrent executions**, extended data retention, external secret stores, log streaming, and dedicated support with SLA.
  
  ✨Comare n8n to Zapier in our detailed [comparison guide](https://www.softr.io/blog/n8n-vs-zapier).
  
  ## **3\. Zapier** — best for quick automations that connect everyday tools
  
  ![Zapier user interface](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/69297d2863bbb29fe5463be9_zapier-interface.webp)
  
  [Zapier](https://zapier.com/) user interface
  
  Zapier is one of the most widely used no-code automation platforms, letting teams link apps and automate repetitive tasks without writing a line of code. With a simple trigger-and-action model (“Zaps”), Zapier moves data and actions between tools like Gmail, Slack, CRM systems, and project apps in the background so you don’t have to handle repetitive steps yourself. Its strength is breadth of integrations and ease of use. You can build automations fast, but it’s less suited for deeper, AI-enabled workflows or custom business tools compared to platforms like Softr.
  
  ### **Zapier pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Huge integration ecosystem:** Connect over 8,000+ apps including communication, CRM, support, and productivity tools.
  - **No-code automation:** Build automations visually with templates or step-by-step builders without Dev help.
  - **AI workflow helpers:** Zapier Copilot and AI tools assist with building and optimizing automations.
  - **Unlimited automations:** Even free plans let you create unlimited “Zaps” (workflows).
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **Task-based pricing gets expensive:** Plans limit monthly “tasks” (executed actions), and heavy automation can drive costs up quickly as teams scale.
  - **Basic business logic only:** Zapier’s trigger–action model handles linear tasks well, but for complex logic, AI feedback loops, or cross-tool workflow enforcement, it’s less capable than tools built for those jobs.
  - **Free plan limits:** Free accounts are capped at 100 tasks/month and two-step automations, restricting real use for teams.
  
  ### **Zapier best features**
  
  - **Visual automation builder:** Drag-and-click workflow creation with conditional logic and branching.
  - **Broad app support:** One of the largest libraries of integrations across business apps and platforms.
  - **Automation templates:** Prebuilt workflows help you get started fast.
  - **AI helpers & agents:** Built-in AI features assist in drafting, troubleshooting, and iterating automations.
  
  ### **Zapier pricing**
  
  Zapier’s pricing is centered around _monthly task limits_ and feature sets.
  
  - **Free:** $0 — _100 tasks/month_, unlimited Zaps, basic workflows, single user, 15-minute polling.
  - **Professional:** $15.23/month (billed annually after free trial) — _750 tasks/month_, multi-step workflows, premium apps, logic tools.
  - **Team:** $52.58/month (billed annually) — Everything in Pro plus shared folders, collaboration tools, roles/permissions, SAML SSO.
  - **Enterprise:** Custom pricing — Organization-level security, governance, analytics, and support.
  
  _Note:_ Overages or higher task tiers can drive up cost quickly as automation use grows, especially for mid-sized teams.
  
  ✨ Looking for alternatives? Visit our in-depth [Zapier alternatives](https://www.softr.io/blog/best-zapier-alternatives) guide.
  
  ## **4\. Fathom** — best for automatically capturing meeting notes, summaries, and action items
  
  ![Fathom AI notetaker](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/696de7f1f81818753ec93158_fathom.webp)
  
  [Fathom AI notetaker](https://www.fathom.ai/)
  
  Fathom is an AI meeting assistant that records, transcribes, and summarizes your Zoom, Google Meet, or Microsoft Teams calls so you can stay focused on the conversation instead of jotting down minutes. Its core value is eliminating manual note-taking and turning meetings into clear, structured minutes and action plans you can search and share later. It works quietly in the background, captures meeting context, highlights key moments, and delivers summaries and action items automatically, making it a time-saver for teams that live in virtual meetings.
  
  ### **Fathom pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Unlimited recordings & transcription:** You can record and transcribe every virtual meeting you join without hitting minutes caps.
  - **Instant AI summaries:** After a call ends, Fathom generates readable summaries and highlights without extra steps.
  - **Action items & integrations:** AI-detected action items plus integration with Slack, CRM tools, and more help push work forward.
  - **Searchable meeting library:** Search across transcripts and summaries to find what you need later.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **No mobile app:** Recording and AI features are tied to desktop/web apps, which can be limiting for hybrid teams.
  - **AI summaries restricted on free plan:** Free only gives a handful of advanced summaries per month; full AI insights require paid tiers.
  
  ### **Fathom best features**
  
  - **Automated meeting recording & transcription:** Fathom auto-records and transcribes meetings so you don’t miss context or key details.
  - **AI-generated summaries & highlights:** AI breaks long meetings into short, usable summaries with action points and key moments highlighted.
  - **Action item detection:** AI pulls out tasks and next steps from conversations automatically.
  - **Searchable call archive:** Find insights from past calls by searching keywords across transcripts.
  - **Team collaboration tools (paid):** Shared meeting libraries, folders, and comment threads help teams stay aligned.
  
  ### **Fathom pricing**
  
  Pricing varies based on individual or team use, with generous free options and progressively advanced paid tiers:
  
  - **Free:** $0 — Unlimited recordings & transcription; limited AI summaries and action items per month.
  - **Premium:** $20/month per user — Unlimited advanced AI summaries, action items, custom summary formats, and Ask Fathom.
  - **Team:** $18/month per user — Adds shared meeting libraries, global search, team collaboration, playlists, and keyword alerts.
  - **Business:** $28/month per user — CRM field sync, deal overview insights, coaching scorecards, and more enterprise-grade features.
  
  Note: Pricing can vary slightly by billing cycle and discounts for annual plans.
  
  ## Visuals & presenting
  
  ## **1\. Figma Make** — best for generating UI layouts and design starting points from prompts
  
  ![Figma Make](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/696deedd76d7f61b13b08046_figma-make.webp)
  
  [Figma Make](https://www.figma.com/make/) interface
  
  Figma Make is Figma’s AI-powered prompt-to-app tool that helps you turn ideas and existing design context into interactive prototypes, UI layouts, and even web app previews using natural language. Instead of building screens or interactions from scratch, you describe what you need,  like a dashboard, form flow, or product layout, and Figma Make uses AI to generate a working foundation you can refine or hand off to engineers. It’s built right into the Figma environment so teams can go from idea to interactive design fast without switching tools.
  
  ### **Figma Make pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Prompt-driven UI & prototype creation:** Turn simple text prompts into structured layouts and interactive prototype previews without starting from blank canvas.
  - **Leverages real design context:** You can attach frames, components, or design systems to guide the AI’s output, keeping generated screens on-brand and consistent.
  - **Integrated into Figma workflows:** Works alongside standard Figma design, FigJam, and Slides tools, keeping everything in one workspace.
  - **Interactive outcomes:** Outputs aren’t just static layouts: they can behave like live prototypes that you can test and refine.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **Not a full design suite on its own:** You still rely on Figma’s design tools for detailed layout tweaks and visual polish.
  - **Feature access varies by plan:** Full publishing and team collaboration depend on paid Figma plans with “Full seats.”
  - **AI credits may apply:** Heavy use of Make and other Figma AI features can consume AI credits depending on task complexity and underlying model choices.
  
  ### **Figma Make best features**
  
  - **Prompt-to-prototype build:** Describe an interface or interaction in plain language and get a running example you can test and iterate.
  - **Design attachment support:** Attach existing frames or components into the prompt to guide outputs and maintain style consistency.
  - **Interactive preview & iteration:** You can preview clickable flows or prototypes and refine them via AI suggestions or manual edits.
  - **Team collaboration:** Files created with Figma Make can be shared and reviewed like any other Figma file (permissions vary by plan).
  
  ### **Figma Make pricing**
  
  Figma Make is included as part of Figma’s broader product suite — it isn’t sold as a separate subscription. Access depends on your Figma plan and seat type:
  
  - **Free (Starter):** Limited access; you can experiment with Figma Make drafts, but team publishing and advanced features require paid plans. Starter users can share up to three Figma Make files with collaborators.
  - **Professional (~$15/editor/month billed annually):** Full access to Figma Make as part of the design workflow, including team libraries and full AI feature sets.
  - **Organization (~$45/editor/month billed annually):** Adds advanced team governance, SSO, analytics, and higher AI usage quotas (including Figma Make).
  
  Note: AI usage in Figma Make may draw on Figma’s AI credit system, where higher-end operations or heavy use can consume more credits.
  
  ## **2\. Nano Banana — best for generating visual assets quickly**
  
  ![Nanobanana Gemini](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/696df4539494dd72b5323dd9_gemini-nano-banana.webp)
  
  [Gemini Nano Banana](https://gemini.google.com/app?android-min-version=301356232&ios-min-version=322.0&is_sa=1&campaign_id=gemini_overview_page&utm_source=gemini&utm_medium=web&utm_campaign=gemini_overview_page&pt=9008&mt=8&ct=gemini_overview_page&hl=en-CA&_gl=1*t1adlr*_gcl_au*Njc3MzY4Mzc3LjE3Njg4MTIzMzI.*_ga*NDUwMzkzMjE5LjE3Njg4MTIzMzQ.*_ga_WC57KJ50ZZ*czE3Njg4MTIzMzMkbzEkZzEkdDE3Njg4MTI2OTEkajU0JGwwJGgw)
  
  Nano Banana refers to Google’s official AI image generation and editing model, known technically as Gemini 2.5 Flash Image. It runs inside Google’s Gemini products (Gemini app, AI Studio, Vertex AI and related tools) and lets you create or revise images using natural language and image prompts. It’s good for creating visual content rapidly, though it’s _not_ a full slide deck app on its own.
  
  This model and its higher-end sibling Nano Banana Pro (built on Gemini 3 Pro Image) excels at generating clear, context-aware visuals you can then place into presentations, marketing assets, social visuals, etc.
  
  ### **Nano Banana pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Fast visual generation:** Turn text or reference images into usable visual assets in seconds.
  - **Natural-language editing:** Adjust visuals by describing changes, making iterations easier without traditional design tools.
  - **Versatile for content creation:** Great for generating graphics, concept imagery, and illustrations you can drop into slides or docs.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **Not a slide editor:** What you get are images, not complete presentation files; you still assemble slides in PowerPoint, Google Slides, or similar tools.
  - **Official pricing depends on how you access it:** Nano Banana usage through Google Gemini or API has its own pricing (often per image/token), and third-party credit-based packages vary widely.
  - **May need refinement:** You’ll often tweak layouts, compositional balance and context manually after generation.
  
  ### **Nano Banana best features**
  
  - **Prompt-based visual assets:** Describe what you need and get graphics ready for presentations or social posts.
  - **Context-aware image editing:** Keeps elements (like characters, objects, style) consistent across outputs.
  - **Iterative refinement:** Change visuals with simple text edits without rebuilding from scratch.
  - **High-quality generation:** Especially with Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image), you get better resolution and more detailed imagery.
  
  ### **Nano Banana pricing**
  
  Nano Banana isn’t sold as a standalone product. Pricing depends on how you access Google’s Gemini image models.
  
  Free (limited)
  
  - Limited image generation via the Gemini app and Google AI Studio.
  - Daily caps apply and can change.
  
  **Google AI Pro (subscription)**
  
  - $19.99/month
  - Higher image-generation limits in Gemini.
  - Access to advanced Gemini models, including higher-quality image generation.
  
  **Gemini API / Vertex AI (pay-as-you-go)**
  
  - Nano Banana (Gemini 2.5 Flash Image): ~$0.039 per image
  - Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image):
    - ~$0.13 per image (standard resolution)
    - Up to ~$0.24 per image (high-resolution outputs)
  
  ## **3\. Canva AI Presentations** — best for generating complete presentation drafts from prompts
  
  ![Canva AI presentations](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/696df5b5e0b27165ed97e592_create_ai-presentation-maker_lead.webp)
  
  [Canva AI](https://www.canva.com/create/ai-presentations/)
  
  Canva’s AI presentation tools are part of its broader AI-powered design suite (“Magic Design”), letting you quickly turn ideas, outlines, or uploaded docs into presentations with structured slides, visuals, and copy using AI assistance. Instead of building slides by hand, you describe what you want, like a pitch deck or training deck, and Canva suggests layouts, styles, and content you can refine visually in its editor. AI’s suggestions are backed by Canva’s huge template library and design system, making it easier for non-designers to build polished decks fast.
  
  ### **Canva AI Presentations pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Prompt-based slide creation:** Use AI to generate a full deck from a text prompt, outline, or uploaded document.
  - **Design ecosystem:** Pick from thousands of templates, illustrations, icons, and media assets to elevate slides instantly.
  - **Real-time collaboration:** Teams can edit, comment, and present together in the cloud.
  - **Multi-format export:** Download decks as PDF, PNG, JPEG or export to PowerPoint formats.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **AI output still needs polishing:** Generated slides often need layout tweaks, visual adjustments, and copy refinement before they’re presentation-ready.
  - **AI feature limits on free plan:** Free accounts have limited access to AI tools like Magic Design and may run out of free generations quickly.
  
  ### **Canva AI Presentations best features**
  
  - **AI deck generation:** Type a prompt or outline and get a structured slide deck with suggested layouts and content.
  - **Template + asset library:** Millions of design templates, stock media, charts, and icons to speed creative quality.
  - **Realtime team editing:** Built-in collaboration lets teams refine and finalize slides together.
  - **AI copy and visuals:** Canva’s Magic Write and image tools generate text and visuals that match your theme.
  
  ### **Canva pricing**
  
  Canva offers per-person pricing with plans for individuals, teams, and enterprises. AI presentation features are included in paid plans, with usage limits that vary by tier.
  
  - **Free — €0/year (1 person):**
  - Basic editor, limited templates and assets, and restricted AI features.
  - **Pro — €110/year per person:**
  - Premium templates and assets, Brand Kits, higher AI usage, and advanced design tools. Free trial available.
  - **Business — €160/year per person:**
  - Built for teams. Adds collaboration tools, approvals, shared assets, higher AI limits, and admin controls. Free trial available.
  - **Enterprise — Custom pricing:**
  - Organization-wide controls, SSO/SCIM, advanced security, custom integrations, and dedicated support.
  
  **Notes:**
  
  - Pricing is per user, billed yearly (monthly toggle available).
  - AI features (including AI presentations) are included, but usage limits scale by plan.
  - Enterprise pricing depends on seat count and requirements.
  
  ## Writing, research, notes
  
  ## **1\. QuillBot(extension enabled)** — best for rewriting, paraphrasing, or simplifying text
  
  ![Quillbot](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/696df8786416ff92a80eec52_quillbot.webp)
  
  [QuillBot](https://quillbot.com/)
  
  QuillBot is an AI writing assistant built to help teams rewrite, clarify, and polish text quickly without leaving your workflow. It’s used for editing drafts, simplifying language, checking grammar, and summarizing content — ideal when you want clearer, more concise writing without drafting from scratch. It integrates well with browsers and editors so you can improve writing directly in email, docs, or web editors.
  
  ### **QuillBot pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Paraphrasing & refinement:** Rewrite or rephrase text to improve clarity, tone, and flow.
  - **Multiple writing tools in one place:** Grammar checker, summarizer, tone analysis, plagiarism checking, citation tools, and translation.
  - **Integrated in workflows:** Works via web interface and browser extension so you can edit where you work.
  - **Helps with SEO and readability:** Paraphrasing can improve keyword integration and readability without rewriting manually.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **Not a creator of original structured content:** QuillBot refines text you provide: it doesn’t generate fully structured articles or workflows like tools built for product content or database logic.
  - **Free limits on rewrite modes and length:** Free users see word caps and fewer paraphrasing modes; Premium unlocks full capabilities.
  - **Still requires review:** AI suggestions often need human editing for tone precision, accuracy, and context.
  
  ### **QuillBot best features**
  
  - **AI Paraphraser with multiple styles:** Choose from modes like Standard, Fluency, Creative, or Formal to rephrase text your way.
  - **Grammar & tone tools:** Check and adjust readability, correctness, and audience fit.
  - **Summarization & citation tools:** Condense long text into key points and generate citations.
  - **Browser and editor integration:** Enhance writing directly in Gmail, Docs, and other apps.
  
  ### **QuillBot pricing**
  
  QuillBot uses a freemium model with more features on paid plans:
  
  - **Free:** $0 — Basic paraphrasing and core writing tools with caps on word count per feature.
  - **Premium:** ~$19.95/month (or ~$8.33/month billed annually) — Unlimited words, all paraphrasing modes, plagiarism checker, higher summarizer limits.
  - **Team:** Custom per-seat plans with centralized billing and team management features.
  
  ## **2\. Obsidian** — best for building a personal or team knowledge system with linked notes
  
  ![Obsidian interface](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/696df8effe60badbcd5a7073_obsidian.webp)
  
  [Obsidian](https://obsidian.md/)
  
  Obsidian is a Markdown-based knowledge management and note-taking app focused on helping you connect ideas over time. Instead of treating notes as isolated pages, Obsidian lets you link thoughts, documents, and concepts into a graph that reveals relationships across your knowledge. It’s popular with writers, researchers, and knowledge workers who want full control of their info and the ability to extend it with plugins and custom workflows.
  
  ### **Obsidian pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Link-first knowledge graph:** Obsidian visualizes connections between notes so you can see patterns and relationships (the “second brain” effect).
  - **Local-first Markdown files:** Your notes are standard files you control and can sync or back up however you like.
  - **Extensible ecosystem:** Plugins add calendars, tasks, graph filters, AI integrations, and more.
  - **Free core features:** You don’t need to pay to use the core note-taking, linking, and graph tools.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **Steep learning curve:** A powerful system means many settings and options, and mastery takes practice compared to simple note apps.
  - **Manual structure required:** You build note networks yourself; there’s no automatic summarization or insight extraction like AI tools provide.
  - **No native AI summarization:** Core Obsidian doesn’t automatically read and summarize files — you rely on plugins or external tools for that.
  
  ### **Obsidian best features**
  
  - **Interactive graph view:** Visualize how ideas and notes connect across your vault.
  - **Rich plugin marketplace:** Add advanced features like task boards, spaced repetition, and AI query plugins.
  - **Cross-platform support:** Works on macOS, Windows, Linux, iOS, and Android.
  - **Markdown at the core:** Standard text files that stay yours and easy to export or migrate.
  
  ### **Obsidian pricing**
  
  Obsidian’s core note-taking and knowledge-linking app is free to use with no required subscription.
  
  - **Free:** $0 — Full Obsidian app, unlimited local notes, graph links, plugins, community features.
  - **Obsidian Sync:** $4/month per user (billed annually) or ~$5/month (monthly) — Secure cross-device sync.
  - **Obsidian Publish:** $8/month per site (billed annually) or ~$10/month (monthly) — Host notes online.
  - **Catalyst:** One-time $25 — Optional perks and early access builds.
  
  The free plan includes all core functionality; paid add-ons are optional services rather than required tiers.
  
  ## **3\. ChatGPT — best for general-purpose writing, research, and reasoning support**
  
  ![ChatGPT 5.2 interface](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/696dfa986416ff92a80f6bd5_chatGPT.webp)
  
  [ChatGPT](https://chatgpt.com/)
  
  ChatGPT is a conversational AI assistant designed to help individuals and teams think, write, research, and problem-solve faster. It’s often the first AI tool teams adopt because it’s flexible: you can use it to draft emails, outline content, summarize documents, analyze ideas, explain concepts, or brainstorm solutions in plain language.
  
  Built by OpenAI, ChatGPT works best as a thinking and drafting partner rather than an execution engine.
  
  ### **ChatGPT pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Extremely versatile:** Handles writing, editing, summarization, research, ideation, and reasoning in one interface.
  - **Low barrier to entry:** No setup required: start typing and get responses immediately.
  - **Strong drafting support:** Useful for emails, outlines, explanations, and first-pass content.
  - **Continuously improving models:** Access to newer models improves reasoning, clarity, and context handling over time.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **Not connected to your workflows by default:** Doesn’t update records, trigger actions, or enforce processes without custom integrations.
  - **Context lives in chat, not systems:** Outputs must be copied into docs, tools, or workflows manually.
  - **Not a source of truth:** Responses still need review for accuracy, especially for factual or sensitive work.
  
  ### **ChatGPT best features**
  
  - **Conversational writing & editing:** Draft, rewrite, and refine text with natural back-and-forth.
  - **Summarization & explanation:** Break down long documents or complex topics quickly.
  - **Reasoning & problem-solving:** Think through scenarios, plans, or decisions step by step.
  - **Multimodal inputs (paid plans):** Work with text, images, files, and data in one interface.
  - **Custom GPTs (paid plans):** Create task-specific assistants with instructions and knowledge.
  
  ### **ChatGPT pricing**
  
  ChatGPT uses a freemium model with optional upgrades for more advanced capabilities:
  
  - **Free:** $0 — limited messages, reasoning, and uploads
  - **Go:** $7/month — more access to GPT-5, higher limits
  - **Plus:** $20/month — advanced reasoning, faster responses, expanded tools
  - **Pro:** $200/month — full access, highest limits, priority features
  - **Business:** $25/user/month (annual) — shared workspace, admin controls, no training on company data
  - **Enterprise:** Custom — enterprise security, compliance, and support
  
  **Bottom line:** Great value for individual knowledge work; costs scale quickly for teams and heavy usage.
  
  ## Email
  
  ## **1\. Goblin** — best for drafting and replying to emails faster with AI
  
  ![Goblin tools ](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67a3700c65457964cf349cd4/696dfe81bdd96c2dce17b669_goblin-tools.webp)
  
  [Goblin tools](https://goblin.tools/)
  
  Goblin (often called Goblin Tools) is a lightweight, AI-powered set of tools that helps you break down tasks, simplify writing, adjust tone, and draft better emails without much setup. It’s not a full email client or workflow automation platform; it’s a work-assist suite you can use when you need quick clarity or structure for writing and thinking tasks. Goblin’s tools include functions like turning brain-dumps into structured actions, evaluating emotional tone, and rephrasing text to fit your intent: useful when crafting professional emails, summaries, or task lists.
  
  ### **Goblin pros and cons**
  
  **Pros**
  
  - **Free to use:** The core Goblin Tools suite is free online, and keeps AI tools accessible without paywalls.
  - **Multiple writing helpers:** Built-in tools like Formalizer (tone adjustment) and Compiler (structure builder) can help refine email drafts.
  - **Task breakdown and idea refinement:** Tools like Magic To-Do turn rough thoughts into actionable steps.
  - **Mobile apps available:** Optional apps on Android and iOS make it convenient on the go.
  
  **Cons**
  
  - **Not a full email client:** Goblin doesn’t send or manage email; it helps you write and structure email text only.
  - **No deep integrations:** There’s no connection to inboxes, CRMs, or workflow tools: you manually copy output into your systems.
  - **Output quality varies:** AI suggestions can be rough and still require review for professional tone and accuracy.
  - **Limited team features:** It’s primarily a personal tool — there’s no native team collaboration or sharing for workflows.
  
  ### **Goblin best features**
  
  - **Tone adjustment (Formalizer):** Transform your draft to sound more professional, casual, assertive, or empathetic.
  - **Task breakdown (Magic To-Do):** Turn a high-level goal into clear smaller steps.
  - **Compiler for clarity:** Organize messy thoughts or paragraphs into a coherent summary.
  - **Judge (tone detector):** Quickly check how an email’s emotional tone comes across.
  
  ### **Goblin pricing**
  
  - **Free:** The core web tool remains free with all main features accessible in-browser.
  - **Mobile & Pro options:** In-app purchases and a **Pro subscription (≈$11.99/month, or ~$22.99/year)** unlock additional convenience and remove usage caps on mobile.
  
  ## **2\. Superhuman** —  best for high-volume inbox management with AI-assisted replies, summaries, and prioritization
  
